1775875548896912	vessel-dev	itc:v3:AWLJkn-SeSTkkkQAAAAAQdav9XquqoAAAAEyCA		item.create	bn-2q7	{"description":"Between bind_unix_listener and set_permissions(0o600) in src/server/mod.rs:122-130, the Unix socket briefly exists with default perms (0o755 after umask). Local attacker could connect during the window and issue any protocol request (Spawn/GetEnv/Snapshot/Kill). Mitigated on /run/user/$UID (systemd 0o700 parent) but fully exposed on /tmp/vessel-$UID.sock fallback. Fix: wrap bind in umask(0o077) restore, or bind inside a pre-created 0o700 per-UID dir, or bind-and-rename. Severity: Medium. CWE-732/CWE-367. See SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md [M-1].","kind":"task","title":"security: close socket permission TOCTOU window"}	blake3:n043uCn7jU-z0_HxPTO9DlvlsbfhP5MqCV42QufqSx4
1775875553512355	vessel-dev	itc:v3:AWLJkn-SeSTkkkQAAAAAQdav9XquqoAAAAEyCQ		item.create	bn-1om	{"description":"src/client.rs:53-60 falls back to /tmp/vessel-$UID.sock when /run/user/$UID is unavailable (non-systemd hosts, containers, sandboxes). /tmp is world-traversable and compounds the M-1 TOCTOU. Fix: create /tmp/vessel-$UID/ with mode 0700 first, place the socket inside, verify ownership and mode before bind/connect, reject if dir is foreign-owned or has wider perms. Severity: Low. CWE-377. See SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md [L-1]. Depends on or pairs with M-1.","kind":"task","title":"security: harden /tmp socket fallback with per-UID 0700 directory"}	blake3:1zMSqQ1JK5rKrYZHh6F4WonzpdgnvzJDCUKITo0lBdk
1775875557743018	vessel-dev	itc:v3:AWLJkn-SeSTkkkQAAAAAQdav9XquqoAAAAEyCg		item.create	bn-agu	{"description":"cargo-audit is not installed locally and not wired into Justfile/CI, so transitive CVE advisories in the dep tree are unverified. Top-level deps are modern (tokio 1.49, clap 4.5, nix 0.31, opentelemetry 0.31) but we have no authoritative signal. Fix: document cargo install cargo-audit in contributor setup, add 'cargo audit' (and optionally cargo deny) to 'just check' and any CI workflow. Severity: Low (advisory). See SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md [L-2].","kind":"task","title":"security: add cargo audit to CI and just check"}	blake3:MOI60KpGNjLw-mpn0LsAadImKF353HymS_0QObQ3RNg
1775875562073448	vessel-dev	itc:v3:AWLJkn-SeSTkkkQAAAAAQdav9XquqoAAAAEyCw		item.create	bn-26r	{"description":"Transcript ring (src/server/transcript.rs) and virtual screen (src/server/screen.rs) store raw PTY bytes; Dump and Snapshot return them to any socket-authorized client. If a spawned agent echoes an API key or password prompt, it lands in the transcript and any --record artifact. Inherent to a PTY runtime but undocumented. Fix: add a 'Data capture' section to README.md / docs/ warning users away from spawning interactive credential flows (ssh password, sudo -S, cloud CLI login) under vessel spawn --record. Optional follow-up: --no-transcript flag for sensitive agents. Severity: Informational. See SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md [I-1].","kind":"task","title":"docs: warn that PTY transcripts capture credentials verbatim"}	blake3:fKZOv38eFO-M_cEorp60Pu7x7Io_bQRDOXVeX0Yrq-Q
