1776816272450656	vessel-dev	itc:v3:AWLJkn-SeSTkkkQAAAAAQdav9XquqoAAAAEyDQ		item.create	bn-27a	{"description":"## Summary\n\n`Server::run` in `src/server/mod.rs:122` binds the Unix listener with the default umask, then tightens permissions to `0o600` a few instructions later via `std::fs::set_permissions` (line 128-129). During that window the socket exists on disk with loose perms (typically 0o755/0o775 minus umask, e.g. 0o644 or 0o664).\n\nA local user who can traverse the socket's parent directory can `connect()` during the race window and issue `Request`s. The server has no in-band authentication — all access control is file-system permissions — and `Spawn` requests execute arbitrary commands as the vessel user. Flagged by Snitch as CWE-367 / A01:2021 (Medium).\n\n## Real impact\n\nDepends on the parent directory:\n\n- **Default path** `/run/user/$UID/vessel.sock`: `/run/user/$UID` is mode 0700 on systemd Linux, so no other local user can traverse in. Race is effectively unexploitable here.\n- **Fallback path** `/tmp/vessel-$UID.sock` (used when `/run/user/$UID` does not exist — non-systemd, some BSDs, stripped containers): `/tmp` is world-traversable. Race window is genuinely exploitable → local privilege escalation to the vessel user's UID via arbitrary `Spawn`.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nSet a restrictive umask (`0o177`) immediately before `bind_unix_listener` and restore it afterwards so the socket is created owner-only atomically. Keep the explicit `set_permissions(0o600)` as belt-and-suspenders. Consider also refusing to bind when the parent directory is not owner-only (addresses the related Low TOCTOU finding at line 99 as defense-in-depth).\n\n## Secondary (Low) finding to note but not fix now\n\nSnitch also flagged `src/server/mod.rs:99` as TOCTOU between `symlink_metadata` and the subsequent `remove_file`/`bind`. Current code is safe because `remove_file` operates on the symlink itself and AF_UNIX `bind()` does not follow symlinks — but the check-then-use pattern is fragile under future refactors. Worth a comment in code and/or the parent-dir-mode check, not a full rewrite to openat/unlinkat.\n\n## References\n\n- Scan report: `ws/default/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md`\n- Tool: Snitch","kind":"bug","labels":["security"],"size":"s","title":"Race window between Unix socket bind and 0o600 chmod on fallback path"}	blake3:5_IMqmxdWf066kenChO9rCEmVlX3tYfFPLwLdMp4dyk
